      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe key point is that the Hub never holds the API key in its own process environment. Instead, a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the child process\u0027s environment. The same approach applies to the Query agent as well \u2014 it receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from or present in the Hub\u0027s process environment.\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key only exists inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5413,
      "output_tokens": 183
    }
